{"question_id": "V2-dev-BOOK-en-T2-002", "approach": "LEX5B", "approach_base": "LEX5B", "flags": {}, "setting": "en-en", "q_lang": "en", "d_lang": "en", "corpus": "K", "corpus_set": "BOOK_en", "answer_text": "Mrs. Auld first taught him the alphabet and to spell short words, but Mr. Auld forbade her to continue, saying it was unlawful and unsafe to teach a slave to read and that learning would spoil a slave, make him unmanageable, and unfit him to be a slave (Chapter VI). Douglass then made friends of little white boys in the street, converting them into teachers, and took his book on errands, finishing his lessons quickly to find time to study (Chapter VII). Mr. Auld's words also revealed to Douglass the pathway from slavery to freedom (Chapter VI).", "abstained": false, "retrieved_units": [{"text": "[stripped: 1011 chars]", "doc_id": "K.gutenberg-23_douglass_narrative.en", "section_id": "K.gutenberg-23_douglass_narrative.en::o011", "unit_ids": ["K.gutenberg-23_douglass_narrative.en::p1_b109", "K.gutenberg-23_douglass_narrative.en::p1_b110"], "kind": "package", "score": null, "rank": null, "span": [76319, 77330], "meta": {"chunk": 5734, "completed": 14, "prefix": 0, "provenance": [["K.gutenberg-23_douglass_narrative.en", 76319, 77330, "body"]]}}, {"text": "[stripped: 1027 chars]", "doc_id": "K.gutenberg-23_douglass_narrative.en", "section_id": "K.gutenberg-23_douglass_narrative.en::o012", "unit_ids": ["K.gutenberg-23_douglass_narrative.en::p1_b115", "K.gutenberg-23_douglass_narrative.en::p1_b116"], "kind": "package", "score": null, "rank": null, "span": [84391, 85418], "meta": {"chunk": 5746, "completed": 140, "prefix": 0, "provenance": [["K.gutenberg-23_douglass_narrative.en", 84391, 85418, "body"]]}}, {"text": "[stripped: 799 chars]", "doc_id": "K.gutenberg-23_douglass_narrative.en", "section_id": "K.gutenberg-23_douglass_narrative.en::o012", "unit_ids": ["K.gutenberg-23_douglass_narrative.en::p1_b113"], "kind": "package", "score": null, "rank": null, "span": [819