{"question_id": "V2-dev-BOOK-en-T3-001", "approach": "LEX5B", "approach_base": "LEX5B", "flags": {}, "setting": "en-en", "q_lang": "en", "d_lang": "en", "corpus": "K", "corpus_set": "BOOK_en", "answer_text": "Franklin's father made candles from tallow. According to Faraday, tallow is the suet, or fat of the ox (Russian tallow, in the dips he showed). To convert it into stearin, the fat or tallow is first boiled with quick-lime to make a soap, which is then decomposed by sulphuric acid; the acid removes the lime, leaving the fat re-arranged as stearic acid, with glycerin produced at the same time. The oil is then pressed out, and the remaining substance is melted and cast into candles.", "abstained": false, "retrieved_units": [{"text": "[stripped: 759 chars]", "doc_id": "K.gutenberg-20203_franklin_autobiography.en", "section_id": "K.gutenberg-20203_franklin_autobiography.en::o015", "unit_ids": ["K.gutenberg-20203_franklin_autobiography.en::p1_b82"], "kind": "package", "score": null, "rank": null, "span": [32201, 32960], "meta": {"chunk": 5038, "completed": 0, "prefix": 0, "provenance": [["K.gutenberg-20203_franklin_autobiography.en", 32201, 32960, "body"]]}}, {"text": "[stripped: 1009 chars]", "doc_id": "K.gutenberg-14474_faraday_chemical-history-of-a-candle.en", "section_id": "K.gutenberg-14474_faraday_chemical-history-of-a-candle.en::o029", "unit_ids": ["K.gutenberg-14474_faraday_chemical-history-of-a-candle.en::p1_b41", "K.gutenberg-14474_faraday_chemical-history-of-a-candle.en::p1_b42"], "kind": "package", "score": null, "rank": null, "span": [5422, 6431], "meta": {"chunk": 2540, "completed": 26, "prefix": 0, "provenance": [["K.gutenberg-14474_faraday_chemical-history-of-a-candle.en", 5422, 6431, "body"]]}}, {"text": "[stripped: 1157 chars]", "doc_id": "K.gutenberg-14474_faraday_chemical-history-of-a-candle.en", "section_id": "K.gutenberg-14474_faraday_chemical-history-of-a-candle.en::o029", "unit_ids": ["K.gutenberg-14474_faraday_chemical-history-of-a-candle.en: